# Upstream hermes-agent v0.16.0 dependencies — awaiting upstream fix
# PyJWT 2.12.1 → 2.13.0 (auth bypass via forged JWTs)
CVE-2026-48526
# Starlette 1.0.1 → 1.1.0 (SSRF via UNC paths in StaticFiles)
CVE-2026-48818
# Starlette 1.0.1 → 1.3.1 (form limits silently ignored, DoS)
CVE-2026-54283

# mcp 1.26.0 -> 1.27.2/1.28.1 (MCP Python SDK: HTTP transport session handling,
# experimental task handlers, WebSocket transport). HELD, not fixable here:
# hermes-agent 0.19.0 pins mcp==1.26.0 and is written against the 1.x client
# API. Forcing the fix resolves to mcp 2.1.1 (the MCP 2.x SDK) and breaks the
# import Kagetora depends on:
#   ImportError: cannot import name 'streamablehttp_client'
#                from 'mcp.client.streamable_http'
# Verified by the build-time smoke test, not assumed. Mitigation: the agent runs
# on an internal=true network with no direct egress and reaches every tool
# through the Trentina gateway, so the HTTP/WebSocket transport surface these
# CVEs describe is not exposed. Upstream resolves this in 0.20.x via their MCP
# 2.x SDK migration -- revisit when 0.20/0.21 reach PyPI.
CVE-2026-52869
CVE-2026-52870
CVE-2026-59950

# setuptools 70.3.0 -> 78.1.1 (CVE-2025-47273, path traversal in
# setuptools.PackageIndex). The venv's real setuptools IS patched -- it is
# upgraded to 84.0.0 in the Containerfile and Trivy scans that copy clean.
# Trivy nonetheless reports a second setuptools at 70.3.0 under its aggregate
# "Python" target with no corresponding path in the report summary. Searched
# and NOT found: the runtime base (quay.io/hummingbird/python:3.13, empty
# site-packages), the builder image /usr tree, and a freshly created venv all
# come back clean. Source of the 70.3.0 record is unidentified -- ignoring it
# knowingly rather than pretending it is fixed.
# Exploitability here is close to nil regardless: PackageIndex is only reached
# when pip installs from a remote index, and this container never runs pip at
# runtime. It also has no direct egress -- internal=true network, every tool
# reached through the Trentina gateway.
CVE-2025-47273
